  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at.% Ti to CoCrFeNi will trigger in situ formation of a continuous oxide film during high-temperature sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-induced oxide film will be lubricious.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti addition will reduce coefficient of friction and wear rate relative to undoped CoCrFeNi at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti-doped CoCrFeNi will preserve acceptable tribological performance at room temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 5 at.% Ti is a suitable minor addition for testing the proposed effect.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer will likely have a spinel-type structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide layer will develop preferentially at elevated temperatures through tribo-oxidation of a Ti-containing phase.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti promotes formation of a stable, low-shear-strength oxide film at the sliding interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxide film reduces direct metal-to-metal contact, thereby lowering friction and wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, limited mobility of oxide-forming species will leave the mechanical and tribological performance similar to that of undoped CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At temperatures approaching 800 °C, Ti-doped CoCrFeNi will have noticeably lower coefficient of friction and wear rate than undoped CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7515071::rubric_card::000::16e383e6c2"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, Ti-doped and undoped CoCrFeNi will have comparable tribological performance.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will be effective from room temperature through 800 °C in air under representative sliding loads.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Performance may change substantially when load or environment differs from the selected test conditions.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal Ti concentration and the kinetics of oxide-film development are not established.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
